INT. SKI-JUMP SAUNA - EVENING

Cedar benches. Steam. A tiny window shows the great jump in the dusk, floodlights burning.

SIGRID LAARSEN, 20s, towel round her shoulders, sits hunched on the top bench. ANTTI MAKELA, 30s, sits beside her and doesn't talk. COACH VESA, 60s, pours water on the stones. The hiss fills the room.

Sigrid stares at her feet.

VESA
Fourth.

SIGRID
I know.

VESA
Fourth is a good place.

SIGRID
It's not a medal.

VESA
No.

Antti hands her a water bottle. She doesn't take it. He sets it on the bench between them.

SIGRID
I was ten metres short.

VESA
Wind.

SIGRID
No.

Vesa ladles another scoop. The steam rolls over them. Nobody speaks. Outside, the floodlights flick off one by one.
